# 📦 Kubernetes and Containers

Kubernetes works with containerized applications.

A simplified application structure is:

```text
Application
     │
     ▼
 Container Image
     │
     ▼
 Container
     │
     ▼
    Pod
     │
     ▼
Kubernetes
```

Pods are the basic deployable units that Kubernetes uses for running workloads.

---

# 🌍 Real-World Example

Consider an e-commerce application:

```text
E-Commerce Application
│
├── Frontend
├── Backend API
├── Payment Service
├── Order Service
└── Background Jobs
```

These services can be packaged as containers.

Kubernetes can then help manage the workloads as the application grows.

